TITLE:: RLGraph
summary:: The graph of a relation: distances, shortest walks, walks through every object once
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLRelation, Classes/RLRelationContext, Classes/RLVoiceLeading, Classes/RLWalk, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
The objects of a relation as vertices, an edge wherever the relation holds between two different objects. A graph forgets the names of the steps and keeps who is next to whom; the relation context it came from can name the steps of a path again (link::Classes/RLRelationContext#-wordOf::).

Each edge has a strong::cost::: 1 (the default: distance counts steps), the relation's own values (code::\value::, for a relation of Lawvere costs), or what a rule code::(x, y) -> number:: answers. link::#*voiceLeading:: costs each edge the steps its voices move.

Two distances meet here. On Cube Dance the number of steps between two chords is the least voice leading between them, for all 378 pairs (and for every pair of its analogues in 15, 18 and 24 steps). On the 24 triads joined by P, L, R it is not: equal for 72 pairs of 276; for 216 when an edge costs the semitones it moves.

code::
~cd = RLRelationContext.cubeDance;
~g = ~cd.graph;
~c = ~cd.space.major(0);
~g.neighbours(~c);                               // [C minor, E minor, C aug]
~g.distance(~c, ~cd.space.major(6));             // 6
~g.shortestPaths(~c, ~cd.space.major(1));        // two walks of three steps, through C aug
~g.countHamiltonianCycles;                       // 1296
~g.hamiltonianCycle.collect(_.name);             // the first of them

~cw = RLRelationContext.triads(RLEDO(12));       // the 24 triads; P, L, R
~cw.graph.countHamiltonianCycles;                // 62
~cw.graph.distance(~cw.space.major(0), ~cw.space.major(1));                           // 4 edges
RLGraph.voiceLeading(~cw.union).distance(~cw.space.major(0), ~cw.space.major(1));     // 5 semitones along them
RLVoiceLeading.stepsBetween(~cw.space.major(0), ~cw.space.major(1));                  // 3 directly
::

The search for Hamiltonian cycles is exact, by depth first with forced moves, and meant for graphs of some tens of vertices (Cube Dance takes a few hundredths of a second).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: relation
A relation of one list to itself. Loops are left out.
argument:: cost
nil (1 per edge), code::\value:: (the relation's values), or a Function code::(x, y) -> number::.

METHOD:: voiceLeading
The graph of a relation of chords of one link::Classes/RLEDO::, each edge costing the steps its voices move (link::Classes/RLVoiceLeading#*stepsBetween::).

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: objects
METHOD:: relation

METHOD:: size
METHOD:: edgeCount
The numbers of vertices and of edges (an edge both ways counts once).

METHOD:: isSymmetric
Whether every edge goes both ways.

METHOD:: neighbours
METHOD:: degree
METHOD:: degrees
The objects next to one; how many; for every object.

METHOD:: cost
The cost of the edge from x to y, nil when there is none.

METHOD:: indexOf
The place of an object among the vertices, nil when it is not one.

METHOD:: edges
Every edge as code::[i, j, cost, both ways]::, i and j places among the vertices. An edge that goes both ways is listed once, the smaller place first. What link::Classes/RLChordGraph:: sends to the chord graph page.

METHOD:: distances
The least cost from an object to every object, in the order of link::#-objects:: (inf where no walk leads).

METHOD:: distance
The least cost of a walk from x to y.

METHOD:: shortestPath
One cheapest walk from x to y, as the list of objects it meets, both ends in; nil when no walk leads there.

METHOD:: shortestPaths
Every cheapest walk from x to y.
argument:: x
argument:: y
argument:: max
1000 by default.

METHOD:: diameter
The largest distance between two objects.

METHOD:: components
The parts no edge joins, a list of objects each.

METHOD:: countHamiltonianCycles
The number of walks through every object once that come back to their start. In a symmetric graph a cycle and the same cycle backwards count once.

METHOD:: hamiltonianCycles
The first cycles found, each the list of objects in the order met, the start first.
argument:: start
The first object when nil.
argument:: max
How many to return.

METHOD:: hamiltonianCycle
The first one, or nil.
